{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"pinkish-hominoid-fugu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nThe module-size policy has ONE intended hard gate: 800 LOC per `src/rebar` file, single-sourced\nin `.github/module-size-limit.txt` and LOCKED (changing it needs an administrator override).\n`tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` mirrors that gate in-process and READS THE SAME FILE,\nso gate and test can never disagree. That mirror is correct and stays.\n\nSeparately, five seam tests have accumulated their own hard-coded LOC ceilings BELOW 800. These\nwere added incrementally by agents as per-story acceptance criteria and then left in place as\npermanent ratchets. They are not policy: AGENTS.md states 200-500 as a TARGET and 800 as the cap.\nEncoding a target as a failing assertion turns guidance into a build break.\n\nINVENTORY (verified against the tree):\n\n| file:line | subject | bound |\n|---|---|---|\n| test_structured_run_seam.py:50 | runner.py | < 700 |\n| test_structured_run_seam.py:60 | structured_run.py | < 500 |\n| test_decide_ops_seam.py:64 | decide_ops.py | < 800 (hard-coded) |\n| test_decide_ops_seam.py:66 | workflow_ops.py | <= 560 |\n| test_gate_dispatch_seam.py:55 | gate_dispatch.py | < 700 |\n| test_gate_dispatch_seam.py:149 | orchestrator.py | < 700 |\n| test_plan_review_workflow_ops_seam.py:170 | workflow_ops.py, llm/config.py | < 700 each |\n| test_gate_context_seam.py:65 | gate_context.py | < 800 (hard-coded) |\n| test_gate_context_seam.py:72 | llm/config.py | < 700 |\n\n## Why this is a defect, not a preference\n\n1. **Governance inversion.** The 800 cap is deliberately LOCKED. The stricter bounds that actually\n   bind these files are bare literals in test files any contributor can edit. The tightest\n   constraint is the least governed one.\n2. **It breaks the refactors it exists to encourage.** A multi-commit decomposition necessarily\n   passes through intermediate states where the file has not shrunk yet. Every such commit goes\n   RED across four platform cells and needs a manual `Verified` override. This has now happened\n   twice on this epic's stack (changes 1121/1122 at runner.py 782, and again after a rebase).\n3. **It has already cost a full investigation once.** Bug `3a98-36c9-9f41-42ec` was opened for\n   exactly this, when main's growth made the `<700` target unreachable; it was resolved by doing\n   a seam extraction rather than questioning the bound. runner.py has since drifted back to 699 —\n   a ONE-LINE margin — so the same failure is queued up again.\n4. **The duplication is self-locking.** `test_decide_ops_seam.py:127,130` assert that the literal\n   strings `\"(_WORKFLOW_OPS, _HEADROOM_TARGET)\"` and `\"(_LLM_CONFIG, _HEADROOM_TARGET)\"` appear in\n   another test file's SOURCE TEXT — a test whose only purpose is to prevent removal of the bound.\n5. **The hard-coded 800s are a second, unlocked copy of a locked number**, redundant with the\n   single-sourced mirror in test_module_size_contract.py.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete every sub-800 and hard-coded-800 LOC CEILING on `src/rebar` files from the five seam tests,\nplus the two source-text assertions at test_decide_ops_seam.py:127,130 that lock them in place.\nThe 800 cap remains enforced by the CI gate and by test_module_size_contract.py, which is the\nsingle-sourced mirror and is NOT touched.\n\nKEEP the anti-fragmentation FLOORS (`_SPLIT_FLOOR`/`_FLOOR` = 100). They are a different rule in\nthe opposite direction — AGENTS.md's \"never create files < 100 LOC by splitting\" — and are not a\nduplicate of the gate. Each seam test keeps its real subject: that the extraction happened and the\nseam behaves.\n\nThis does NOT retroactively fix intermediate commits already pushed on the current stack; those\nstill need the operator's override. It stops the recurrence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC1: No test under tests/ asserts an upper LOC bound on a `src/rebar` file other than\n  test_module_size_contract.py, which reads the limit from `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n- AC2: No hard-coded LOC ceiling literal (700, 560, 500, or 800) remains in the five seam tests.\n- AC3: The anti-fragmentation floors (100) are retained and still asserted.\n- AC4: The source-text assertions at test_decide_ops_seam.py:127,130 are removed.\n- AC5: Each seam test still asserts its real subject — the extracted module exists and the seam\n  behaves — so no seam loses coverage.\n- AC6: test_module_size_contract.py is unmodified.\n- AC7: make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default selection is green.","id":"db7f-c02c-90ae-4714","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Seam tests duplicate the module-size gate at arbitrary sub-800 thresholds, making guidance a hard build failure"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785644844580457001,"uuid":"f55afdc6-4fba-4b16-9aa9-520c9a71093c"}